# Hand weapons — two different “poses”

## Catalog / sprite pose: `all`

`main-hand` and `off-hand` equipment use **`characterDisplay` bucket `all`** only. Catalog entries use `pose: "all"`. Upload UI uses pose key `all`. Z-index for the weapon sprite uses `poseKey: "all"` + `equipType` / `twoHanded`.

## Body / base-arm stance: real pose keys

Base character parts (`parts.mainHand`, `parts.offHand`) use stance keys such as `1h mainhand`, `1h offhand`, `2h mainhand`, `2h offhand crossbow`, etc. **There is no `mainHand["all"]` arm bucket.**

`derivePoseFromEquipment` must map equipped hand items through **`bodyStancePoseForHandItem()`** — never pass catalog `pose: "all"` through as the body stance.

## Examples

| Equipped item | Catalog pose | Body mainHandPose | Body offHandPose (empty off) |
|---------------|--------------|-------------------|----------------------------|
| 1H rod/sword main | `all` | `1h mainhand` | `1h offhand` |
| 2H polearm main | `all` + `twoHanded` | `2h mainhand` | `2h offhand` |
| Shield off | `all` | (from main or default) | `1h offhand` |

Changing this mapping requires updating **`equipmentPose.test.ts`** and **`basePartsFromApi.test.ts`**, and **user confirmation** per `unit-tests-guard.mdc`.
